contributingGuides/STYLE.md:Our potentially larger collections of data (reports, policies, etc) are typically stored under collection keys. Collection keys let us group together individual keys vs. storing arrays with multiple objects. In general, **do not add a new collection key if it can be avoided**. There is most likely a more logical place to put the state. And failing to associate a state property with its logical owner is something we consider to be an anti-pattern (unnecessary data structure adds complexity for no value).
