docs/articles/expensify-classic/travel/Configure-travel-policy-and-preferences.md:As a Workspace Admin, you can set travel policies for all travel booked under a workspace, including approval methods, flight booking class, and hotel star preferences. You can also create multiple policies with specific conditions for particular groups of employees and/or non-employees.
docs/articles/expensify-classic/travel/Configure-travel-policy-and-preferences.md:Workspace admins can create different travel policies that provide travel rules for different groups of travelers. When using Expensify Travel for the first time, you will need to create a new Travel Policy.
docs/articles/expensify-classic/travel/Configure-travel-policy-and-preferences.md:5. Use the **Edit members** section to select the group of employees that belong to this policy.
docs/articles/expensify-classic/travel/Configure-travel-policy-and-preferences.md:    2. **To add a new policy:** Click **Add new** under Employee or Non-employee in the left menu. Then under the Edit members section, select the group of employees that belong to this policy.
docs/articles/expensify-classic/travel/Configure-travel-policy-and-preferences.md:As a Workspace Admin, you can set travel policies for all travel booked under your workspace, including approval methods, flight booking class, and hotel star preferences. You can also create multiple policies with specific conditions for particular groups of employees and/or non-employees.
docs/articles/expensify-classic/travel/Configure-travel-policy-and-preferences.md:Workspace admins can create different travel policies that provide travel rules for different groups of travelers. When using Expensify Travel for the first time, you will need to create a new Travel Policy.
docs/articles/expensify-classic/travel/Configure-travel-policy-and-preferences.md:5. Use the **Edit members** section to select the group of employees that belong to this policy.
docs/articles/expensify-classic/travel/Configure-travel-policy-and-preferences.md:    2. **To add a new policy:** Click **Add new** under Employee or Non-employee in the left menu. Then under the Edit members section, select the group of employees that belong to this policy.
docs/articles/expensify-classic/expensify-billing/Change-Plan-Or-Subscription.md:Expensify offers various plans depending on your needs: Track, Submit, Collect, Control, and Free. Your choice of plan depends on whether you want to manage your expenses individually or for a group or company. You may need to upgrade from an individual plan to a group plan if you recently hired additional employees that need should be added to a Group Workspace, or you need access to Expensify's features that are only available on a paid plan.
docs/articles/expensify-classic/expensify-billing/Change-Plan-Or-Subscription.md:To upgrade to a group plan, you will need to create a Group Workspace by heading to **Settings > Workspaces > Group** and choosing a Collect or Control plan.
docs/articles/expensify-classic/expensify-billing/Change-Plan-Or-Subscription.md:## I'm on a group policy; do I need the monthly subscription too?
docs/articles/expensify-classic/copilots-and-delegates/Approving-Reports.md:Concierge report approval removes the need for you to manually click "Approve" on endless reports! Instead, you can set up your group Workspace to capture all the requirements you have for your team's expenses. As long as all the rules have been followed and Concierge's additional audit is passed (more below), we will automatically approve such reports on behalf of the approver after submission.
docs/articles/expensify-classic/copilots-and-delegates/Approving-Reports.md:Ensure are a Workspace admin on a group Workspace
docs/articles/expensify-classic/copilots-and-delegates/Approving-Reports.md:Set up your group Workspace so that all of your expense requirements are defined. Setting automatic categories for employees and category rules (e.g., maximum amounts, receipt requirements, etc.) are great examples!
docs/articles/expensify-classic/connect-credit-cards/company-cards/Company-Card-Settings.md:If Scheduled Submit is disabled on the group policy level (or set to a manual frequency), and you have noticed expense reports are still automatically submitted to the group policy, it's likely Scheduled Submit is enabled on the user’s Individual Policy settings.
docs/articles/expensify-classic/connect-credit-cards/company-cards/Troubleshooting.md:If you would like your card programs listed under separate dropdowns, you can select only that group making sure to select all cards from that group each time you are adding a new card.
docs/articles/expensify-classic/connect-credit-cards/Personal-Credit-Cards.md:9. If applicable, you can also map specific Categories and Tags as long as you don't have an integration connection to your default group policy. If you have an integration connected, you'll want to add the Categories and Tags to the expense after the expense is uploaded.
docs/articles/expensify-classic/domains/Domain-Migration.md:3. If you use [Domain Groups](https://help.expensify.com/articles/expensify-classic/domains/Create-A-Group) on your old domain, disable “Restrict Primary Login Selection” on all groups.
docs/articles/expensify-classic/domains/Domain-Migration.md:9. Set up your [domain groups](https://www.google.com/url?q=https://help.expensify.com/articles/expensify-classic/domains/Create-A-Group) on the new domain and add your users to the relevant group.
docs/articles/expensify-classic/domains/Add-Domain-Members-and-Admins.md:- **Domain Admin**: Has full authority over the domain settings and can add or modify members, admin, groups, rules, and company credit cards. Domain Admins are not required to have an email address connected to the domain.
docs/articles/expensify-classic/domains/Add-Domain-Members-and-Admins.md:Once the member verifies their email address, all Domain Admins will be notified and the employee will be added to the default group.
docs/articles/expensify-classic/domains/Claim-And-Verify-A-Domain.md:To complete this step, you must have a Control workspace, and you’ll need access to your domain provider account (GoDaddy, Wix, GSuite, etc.). If you don’t verify the domain, you will still have access to the domain to add and manage credit card expenses and domain admins, but you will not be able to invite members, add groups, use domain reporting tools, set delegates for employees on vacation, or enable SAML SSO. For more guidance on how to complete this process for a specific provider, check the provider’s website.
docs/articles/expensify-classic/domains/Create-A-Group.md:title: Create a group
docs/articles/expensify-classic/domains/Create-A-Group.md:To set different domain rules for different members, you can place them into groups. For example, many organizations create different groups for employees and managers since they generally need different domain permissions.
docs/articles/expensify-classic/domains/Create-A-Group.md:To create a group,
docs/articles/expensify-classic/domains/Create-A-Group.md:5. Select all of the group settings and permissions.
docs/articles/expensify-classic/domains/Create-A-Group.md:   - **Permission Group Name**: Enter a name for the group
docs/articles/expensify-classic/domains/Create-A-Group.md:   - **Default Group**: Determine if new domain members will be automatically added to this group.
docs/articles/expensify-classic/domains/Create-A-Group.md:   - **Strictly enforce expense workspace rules**: Determine if all expense rules must be met before people in this group can submit a report.
docs/articles/expensify-classic/domains/Create-A-Group.md:   - **Restrict primary login selection**: Determine if members of this group will be restricted from using a personal email address to access their Expensify account.
